API confirmed. Pattern for uikit 7.43:

```tsx
import {Button, ToasterComponent, ToasterProvider, Toaster, useToaster} from '@gravity-ui/uikit';

const toaster = new Toaster();

// in component:
const {add} = useToaster();
add({name: 'demo', title: '...', autoHiding: 5000});
```

`autoHiding?: number | false` — timeout in ms after which toast hides itself. Default? Probably some default constant. Let me not bother; pass `autoHiding: 5000` explicitly.

Button in the corner: position fixed bottom-right. Use `--g-*` tokens where possible. Layout via inline styles with position: fixed is fine (no semantic color needed).

Structure:

App.tsx:
```tsx
import {Button, Toaster, ToasterComponent, ToasterProvider, useToaster} from '@gravity-ui/uikit';

const toaster = new Toaster();

function CornerButton() {
  const {add} = useToaster();
  return (
    <Button
      view="action"
      size="l"
      onClick={() => add({name: `toast-${Date.now()}`, title: 'Готово!', content: 'Кнопка нажата', theme: 'success'})}
      style={{position: 'fixed', right: 24, bottom: 24}}
    >
      Показать уведомление
    </Button>
  );
}

export function App() {
  return (
    <ToasterProvider toaster={toaster}>
      <CornerButton />
      <ToasterComponent />
    </ToasterProvider>
  );
}
```

Wait — TOAST_THEMES constant; check themes: likely 'normal' | 'info' | 'success' | 'warning' | 'danger' | 'utility'. autoHiding default — check constants. Also is autoHiding default enabled? Let me check quickly.

